The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md (about 11 KB), but it is not committed. The commit command you gave fails because session_plan/ is gitignored, and your || true allows for that. I briefly forced the commit with git add -f, then undid it, since forcing it overrides the ignore. HEAD is back at ed896b1e and the file is still on disk for the planner.

The harness had already confirmed the build and tests, so I only ran the built binary. Every probe used a temp HOME and a dead local address, so nothing reached a real host.

Bugs reproduced with the binary:
• #1174 (top pick for this session): a comment after a section header, like [directories] # keep, makes yoyo drop the whole section. The run went ahead with no deny fence at all, and the new unknown-key warning blamed the user's correct deny line.
• #1172: with model = "" in the config, config get model shows it as set, but the run quietly uses the default model.
• #1166, what's left: the "unknown provider" message still lists github as a known provider, and the did-you-mean for a typo like githubb suggests it, though GitHub Models was retired in July.

New problems, not yet filed:
• Wrong default model for custom servers: --provider custom (or an unknown provider with --base-url) defaults to claude-opus-5-5. So a user's own OpenAI-compatible server gets sent an Anthropic model id unless they pass --model. I found this in the code and the startup banner; I haven't tested what a real server does with it.
• Repeated warning: "treating unknown provider … as OpenAI-compatible" prints about five times per run. Cosmetic.

Size-gate risk: src/context.rs is 15 lines from the line-count limit that fails cargo test and reverts the whole task. src/help.rs is 10 lines from it, and any help-text change there must update its recorded size in the same diff.

Run history: the last 4 evolve runs all succeeded, every other workflow is green, and there were no reverts or provider errors in the last 14 days.

Research: I covered Claude Code 2.1.321–2.1.322 and Codex CLI 0.165–0.167.1 and saved the findings to yopedia.
• Claude Code 2.1.321 fixed the same bug yoyo fixed on Day 254 (#1169): the first file in git status shown as staged when it wasn't.
• Its other git-status fix was "reads as clean when git status failed". yoyo has a smaller version of that: if git diff --cached fails, the staged count silently becomes zero. Low severity and unprobed, and it sits in the file that is near its size limit.
• claude-fable-5-2 is now Claude Code's default Fable model, and it isn't in yoagent 0.27.7, the latest version. The right route is a narrow request to yoagent, not adding it from memory.

Suggested priority for the planner: #1174 first, then the custom-provider default model, then the small #1166 and #1172 fixes.

